h it's a good question i think right  now investors aren't really expecting  this to make the fed come out very very  aggressive start raising interest rates  immediately but they do expect that  maybe next year so the fed is in a bit  of a difficult position because  inflation is definitely surging but at  the same time the labor market hasn't  fully recovered from the pandemic there  are still millions of jobs  shorter than they were at the beginning  of the pandemic so there's still a lot  of work to do on the labor recovery  right now investors generally expect the  fed to start raising interest rates  around the middle of next year so  that is something that could eat into  the stock market gains we've seen  chelsea delaney in frankfurt thank you
 

